From: Benik3 <benik333@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:46:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sdupdate: verify the image before and after flashing

sdupdate erased the flash and wrote whatever fatload left in RAM, then
created the .done flag. No step was checked. A bad SD read, a corrupt
image or a failed program all left a flash that does not boot, and the
flag stopped any retry. An autoupdate-uboot.bin larger than the 256K it
erases was also written past the erased area.

A clean file on the PC does not prove the copy U-Boot read, and jz_mmc
could report a read with a CRC error as good (fixed separately).

The full, u-boot-only and custom-file updates now:
- read the file until it matches <file>.sha256sum when that file is on
  the card, otherwise until two reads give the same CRC32, at most 3
  reads, with an mmc rescan after a failed read because it can leave
  the card mid-transfer. The build already writes
  thingino-<camera>.bin.sha256sum next to the image
  (generate_release_artifacts.sh, run by pack); its # comment lines are
  skipped;
- refuse an empty image and one larger than its area: the whole chip
  for a full image, UBOOT_SIZE for autoupdate-uboot.bin;
- refuse an image whose u-boot uImage (after the SPL, at
  CONFIG_UBOOT_OFFSET) or kernel uImage (on a 64K boundary from 0x40000)
  fails its data CRC, or whose u-boot is larger than
  CONFIG_SYS_MONITOR_LEN. That is all the SPL loads: spl_sfc_nor.c
  parses the header at memory address CONFIG_UBOOT_OFFSET instead of
  the copy in flash, so spl_parse_image_header normally finds no magic
  and falls back to that size;
- after erasing the area and writing, read the flash back in 64K chunks
  and rewrite only the chunks that differ, for up to 5 rounds, from the
  verified image still in RAM;
- keep rewriting the bootloader area (the first 320K) until it
  verifies, because the camera does not start again without it;
  Ctrl-C on the console stops this;
- write each step and the result to sdupdate.log on the card, one log
  per sdupdate run.

Nothing is erased when a check before the erase fails, and the .done
flags are written only after a verified flash. When only chunks
outside the bootloader area still differ, the update fails without
.done, and the next boot, from a good bootloader, retries it. A failed
erase falls back to rewriting chunk by chunk, which also recovers from
an erase the chip ignored. The CRC of the image in RAM is checked again
before the result is accepted.

CONFIG_SHA256 builds lib/sha256.c, which U-Boot already carries. It is
left out of the T31LC and XIAOMI_SPL builds, which drop other features
for size and load a fixed CONFIG_SYS_MONITOR_LEN of raw u-boot; there a
.sha256sum on the card is ignored with a note and the two reads decide.

The write command takes the size of the verified read instead of
${filesize}, which loading <file>.sha256sum overwrites. The log has a
fixed 8.3 name because fatwrite takes the short name from the first
dot, so <file>.log would share its short name with <file>.

Signed-off-by: Benik3 <benik333@gmail.com>
---
